Makes an animated gif of one event: one camera image per time bin, played at 24 fps.
The file decides what it is: a file with a "Sim" tree is a simulation, anything else is demonstrator data.
The formatting is the same as CreateCameraImageFromHist (sky on top, SIAB boxes, Sky/Ground line),
with the file name on top and the event and time bin above the camera, changing with each frame.
- data: flipped in both camera axes like the stills, so the sky is on top. The Sky/Ground line goes by
        the night's row ratio (y=11.5 before Oct. 2025, y=8.5 from then on).
- sims: NOT flipped, they are written sky-up already. The Sky/Ground line is the horizon for the tilt
        (SEvent tilt, or the Tilt_ folder in the path): y = 7.5 - (90 - tilt)/0.242, so Tilt_90 puts it
        on the camera centre. It is the same geometry EventCleaning's DrawSimHorizon uses.

How to remake the executable
>./compile_script.sh
(or ./compile_script.sh clean first)

How to run
>./run_script.sh /DataAnalysis/MakeThingsPretty/EventGiFs/EventGifs.txt

or from inside s_cgroup
> ./MakeEventGif /DataAnalysis/MakeThingsPretty/EventGiFs/EventGifs.txt /cedar/

gifs are created in ./Gifs as <Output>_E<event>.gif


Gif list file, one row per request, no spaces:
Output,File,Event,FirstTimeBin,LastTimeBin

- Output: name for the gif, the event number is added to it
- File:   full path, either a merged data file or a sim _tdem.root file
    data: /cedar/DataAnalysis/MergedData/Output/<night>/Merged_....root
    sims: /cedar/simdata/sofiadata/20260827_taudavid/<run>/CARE/Tilt_90.000000/<shower>_tdem.root
- Event:  Test tree entry number, or "all" for every triggered event in the file
          (for sims "all" skips the thrown showers that never triggered, their traces are flat)
- FirstTimeBin,LastTimeBin: optional, leave them off to use the defaults
    data: 225-255 (the pulse sits around bin 239)
    sims: 156-200 (the CARE trace starts at bin 156 of the 512-sample trace, pulses sit around 176-200)

Calibration
- data: the night's flasher calibration from flasher_calibration/Output (CamFlasher44, or CamFlasher on 2025 nights)
        and the SiPM gain of each pixel, pedestal = mean of samples 0-99. Same as EventCleaning.
        Most June 2026 flasher files are all NaN, those pixels come out as 0 PE with a WARNING.
- sims: 24.1 ADC per PE, pedestal = mean of samples 157-166. Same as EventCleaning.

PrintFrameDiagnostics in PlotEventGif.h prints the brightest pixel and camera sum for every frame.
